---
// Promises Kept: what Byron ran on in 2019 and what the ward can check.
---

<section class="promise section-padding" id="the-promise">
  <div class="container promise-content">
    <span class="section-label animate-in" data-i18n="promise.label">Promises Kept</span>
    <h2 class="section-title promise-headline animate-in" data-i18n="promise.headline">He Said He Would. He Did.</h2>

    <div class="promise-story">
      <p class="promise-beat animate-in" data-i18n="promise.beat1">
        In 2019, the 25th Ward closed a 23 year chapter of Danny Solis and elected a teacher and organizer who took no money from developers. Neighbors have been checking the receipts ever since.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="promise-kept">
      <li class="promise-kept-item animate-in" style="--reveal-delay: 0s">
        <h3 class="promise-kept-head"><span class="promise-kept-title" data-i18n="promise.k1_title">Take no developer or corporate money</span></h3>
        <p class="promise-kept-desc" data-i18n="promise.k1_desc">Not one dollar since 2015. Byron has upheld that commitment every year in office, and he has pushed for publicly financed elections so no alderman has to depend on that money.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="promise-kept-item animate-in" style="--reveal-delay: 0.1s">
        <h3 class="promise-kept-head"><span class="promise-kept-title" data-i18n="promise.k2_title">Every Tuesday. Seven years.</span></h3>
        <p class="promise-kept-desc" data-i18n="promise.k2_desc">Ward Night every Tuesday since 2019, including all the way through the pandemic. Masks and sanitizer delivered door to door. An emergency fund of nearly $100,000 for neighbors who qualified for nothing else, including undocumented neighbors.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="promise-kept-item animate-in" style="--reveal-delay: 0.2s">
        <h3 class="promise-kept-head"><span class="promise-kept-title" data-i18n="promise.k3_title">Put zoning back in the neighbors' hands</span></h3>
        <p class="promise-kept-desc" data-i18n="promise.k3_desc">A resident Zoning Advisory Board, with members from every neighborhood in the ward, now weighs in on what gets built. In April 2026 that board reviewed Casa Nayarit, the first 76 permanently affordable homes on the Pilsen lot the city bought after Byron blocked 500 luxury apartments.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="promise-kept-item animate-in" style="--reveal-delay: 0.3s">
        <h3 class="promise-kept-head"><span class="promise-kept-title" data-i18n="promise.k4_title">Deliver, block by block</span></h3>
        <p class="promise-kept-desc" data-i18n="promise.k4_desc">Over 800 units of affordable housing created or preserved. Over $500,000 from the state for violence prevention. Over $1 million for Benito Juarez and other ward schools. Cermak Road repaved, and 311 pushed until the potholes and the streetlights got fixed.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="promise-close animate-in" data-i18n="promise.close">
      Seven years later the list is longer and the promise has not changed. On February 23, 2027, the 25th Ward decides whether the work keeps going.
    </p>

    <a href="#petition" class="btn btn-orange btn-massive animate-in promise-cta" data-i18n="promise.cta">Stand With the 25th Ward</a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .promise {
    background: var(--cream-light);
    border-top: 4px solid var(--blue);
  }

  .promise-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--blue-deeper);
  }

  .promise-headline {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .promise-story {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .promise-beat {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  /* Promises kept: placard headings over plain copy, two up on desktop */
  .promise-kept {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: 900px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .promise-kept-head {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }

  .promise-kept-title {
    display: inline;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--cream-light);
    background: var(--blue-deeper);
    padding: 0.12em 0.4em;
    -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone;
    box-decoration-break: clone;
  }

  .promise-kept-desc {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--gray-700);
  }

  .promise-close {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-top: var(--space-3xl);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--gray-700);
  }

  .promise-cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .promise-kept {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
